# Build output is never tracked. tsdown names shared chunks by content hash, so
# every build rewrote these files and the diff said nothing about the change.
# Publishing is unaffected: `npm pack` runs prepack -> build, and the package's
# `files` field picks `lib` up from the tarball.
lib/

node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
dist/
coverage/
*.log
.env
.DS_Store

# Screenshots are release assets: `screenshots.json` lists them and the
# marketplace card renders from them. These two rules are DEFENSIVE, not
# load-bearing today: nothing above matches `docs/`, so as the repository stands
# they change no outcome. They exist so a future broad rule (`*.png`,
# `assets/`, a catch-all) cannot silently swallow the marketplace images.
!docs/assets/
!docs/assets/*.png
